          ":question/id": "c4dca02e-edf1-5494-a3ee-03c75dee63c5",
          ":question/math-academy-id": "q-113787",
          ":question/problem": "$\\int 2x-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
          ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\int 2x-3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x-\\int 3{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int x\\,\\text{d}x-3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\left(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\right)-3\\left(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}\\right)+C \\\\  & ={x}^{2}-{x}^{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
        }
